---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Contact
description: Get in touch with Frank about IT support and service desk roles.
permalink: /contact/
---
<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 sm:px-8 pt-8 grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12">
  <div class="lg:col-span-7">
    <h1 class="font-display font-extrabold tracking-tight text-6xl sm:text-7xl">Say hello</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-[34rem] text-xl text-mist">Hiring for a service desk or first-line role? Want to tell me my home lab is wrong? Either is fine. I'm based in {{ site.location }} and I reply within a working day, usually faster.</p>

    <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}" class="mt-12 inline-block font-display font-extrabold text-[clamp(1.6rem,4.5vw,3rem)] text-mango underline decoration-4 underline-offset-8 hover:text-coconut break-all">{{ site.email }}</a>

    <ul class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
      <li><a href="{{ site.linkedin }}" class="btn btn-ghost" rel="me noopener">LinkedIn</a></li>
      <li><a href="{{ site.github }}" class="btn btn-ghost" rel="me noopener">GitHub</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <aside class="lg:col-span-4 lg:col-start-9 self-start rounded-[2rem] bg-deep p-8">
    <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl">Why no contact form?</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-mist">Forms need a third party to handle your message. Email doesn't. Fewer moving parts, less to go wrong, no data going anywhere it doesn't need to. Frankly, it's the support person's answer.</p>
  </aside>
</section>
